{"name":"Miracle Elixir","hex":"#617ba6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"miracle","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An event that appears inexplicable by the laws of nature and so is held to be supernatural in origin.","A fortunate outcome that prevails despite overwhelming odds against it."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To affect by a miracle; to work a miracle upon."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/miracle"},{"term":"elixir","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A liquid which converts lead to gold.","A substance or liquid which is believed to cure all ills and give eternal life."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/elixir"}],"entries":[{"title":"Miracle","blocks":[{"text":"A miracle is an event that cannot be explained by natural or scientific laws and accordingly gets attributed to some supernatural or preternatural cause. Various religions often attribute a phenomenon characterized as miraculous to the actions of a supernatural being, especially by a deity, a miracle worker, a saint, or a religious leader."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Miracle","wikidata":"Q170774"},{"title":"Elixir","blocks":[{"text":"An elixir is a sweet liquid used for medical purposes, to be taken orally and intended to cure one's illness. When used as a pharmaceutical preparation, an elixir contains at least one active ingredient designed to be taken orally."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/%C3%89lixir_Raspail_devenu_%C3%A9lixir_Angelo.jpg/330px-%C3%89lixir_Raspail_devenu_%C3%A9lixir_Angelo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elixir","wikidata":"Q7005626"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Tintoretto_-_Miracle_of_the_Slave.jpg/500px-Tintoretto_-_Miracle_of_the_Slave.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https